## Summary

Audited the supplied main revision for structural simplicity, using project guidance, architecture docs, prior audit findings and broad sampling of shared client, store, worker, mail, tools and query/search code. Selected one complete, behavior-preserving simplification in internal/db/searchindex.go.

Before: initial training and incremental updates constructed search-vector placements separately; training paired flat chunk references and cell indices by offset across a second traversal of entries.
Now: trainCentroids computes centroids only, and vectorIndex.update places vectors through the same entry-based loop for initial training, retraining and incremental updates. Removed duplicate placement and offset bookkeeping, preserving deterministic ordering, training thresholds and placement reuse (3 insertions, 19 deletions).

Ten existing search tests passed under timeout 30, repository-wide go vet ./... and diff checks passed, and the completed review had no significant findings. The requested git merge --no-ff --no-commit main reported already up to date; no conflict resolution or additional changes were needed.

Deliberately excluded schema, UI, permission, production-data and deployment changes. Worker scheduling and app-specific formatting were left alone because the inspection found no equally clear consolidation to justify expanding the patch.

